Version 0.5.0 starts from kyr0/defuss-dataview commit
7ff0498e426f1d40ceaeff409f4fb725dbe81223 (package 0.4.0).
That standalone project originated at kyr0/defuss/packages/dataview commit
50aae32aa9aea45612510703e75875ed98aa6386 (package 0.3.1).

Historical implementation and original tests are retained byte-for-byte in
tests/fixtures/ for provenance, not as a promise of behavioral compatibility.
SHA-256 provenance appears in tests/fixtures/provenance.json. Historical
fixtures are excluded from the npm package. Current tests live under src/.

The original MIT license and author attribution are retained. Runtime package
entries have zero dependencies. Development tools are installed from the exact
lockfile. The build additionally writes a real-browser test worker bundle,
artifacts/dbsonl.worker.mjs, containing defuss-dbsonl 0.6.0, defuss-dson 1.5.1
and defuss-storage 0.3.1, all MIT licensed by Aron Homberg (see their LICENSE
files in node_modules/). The worker bundle is not part of the npm package.
